# Runway DLS (connected)

Primary source — hosted Storybook (built DLS v2):

- https://dev-runway-dls.changiairport.com/?path=/docs/introduction--docs
- Local stand-ins in this repo: `src/dls/` (Button, Text, chips, Field/Dropdown, Tabs, Drawer, Alert, Badge)
- Process v4 composes those components

Backup — markdown usage guidelines (not an npm package):

- GitHub: https://github.com/cag-euxui/runway-md-components
- Local clone: `/Users/bell/runway-md-components`
- In this repo: `vendor/runway-md-components` → same clone
- Index: `vendor/runway-md-components/README.md`
- Component docs: `vendor/runway-md-components/docs/**/*.md`

## When building UI

1. Prefer `src/dls/` + tokens in `src/index.css`. Match Storybook variants (B2B `semiRounded`, control heights 44/36/28).
2. If Storybook has no story (SideNav, Card, empty page chrome), use Runway markdown under `docs/` and existing tokens.
3. Common Storybook paths:
   - Buttons / chips: Actions & Interactions
   - Inputs / search: Inputs
   - Checkboxes / radios / toggles: Selections
   - Headers: Page Navigation / AdminHeader
4. This repo does **not** import the private `runway-fe` package — local React + Tailwind that matches the stories.

